by nicolas-grekas at 2026-11-17T17:17:44Z

PR rebased and updated.

A loader that fails when asked for the path can't replace the template error anymore. `Source` serializes as before. Its public constructor is unchanged. Compiled templates use an internal factory for the lazy path.

The goal is reproducible builds. On 3.x, warming the cache of the same app in two directories gives the same file names, as `doc/api.rst` describes. But all the files differ, because they embed the absolute path of their source. With this PR, the files are identical.

Filling the path when an error is built would need the loader at the same moment. It would also make `getSourceContext()->getPath()` empty in prod, which is a BC break.

